* Cyberdeck Modeline Install :EMACS_MECHANISM:S0:
:PROPERTIES:
:ID:       4e7a1c93-6b28-4f50-9d13-8c05b2e7a6f4
:MM_PARENT: none
:MM_ORDER:  80.15
:CATEGORY: the-screen
:END:

The one top-level call that starts the bar.

It has to be its own unit, and it has to be the **last** lane slot. The
composer can only build a row from segments that are already registered,
and segments arrive with the widgets at 80.05–80.13. Calling install from
`engine/setup` (80.2) therefore composes an empty bar; calling it from any
widget composes a partial one, because a later widget would have nothing
re-triggering the compose. So: a unit of its own, after everything.

This file existing at all is the record of an omission. The DSL, the
composer, the segments, the order file, the clobber guard and the clock
timer were all written and verified individually, and the bar still never
appeared, because nothing called install. Everything was green and the
feature was dead. If the bar ever stops showing, check here first:
`manifolding-modeline-install` must have run (called immediately
below and again on `after-init-hook`).

Deferring to `after-init-hook` rather than installing inline is what makes
it safe against a later unit that also touches the format, and it means a
failure here degrades to the stock mode line rather than a broken one.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(defun manifolding-modeline--install-after-init ()
  "Install the bar once Emacs has finished starting.
Deferred because a package loaded during init — display-time,
fly-sparkline, super-save — can still be rewriting mode-line-format when
the units are evaluated."
  (condition-case err
      (manifolding-modeline-install)
    (error
     (message "manifolding-modeline: install failed: %s"
              (error-message-string err)))))

(when (boundp 'after-init-hook)
  (add-hook 'after-init-hook #'manifolding-modeline--install-after-init))
;; Run it now too, so a --batch boot still gets a bar. (Not gated on
;; the hook being non-nil: during init it never is, which used to
;; skip both paths and leave the rows empty forever.)
(manifolding-modeline--install-after-init)
#+end_src
